{"title":"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Test_Errors\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Test Errors</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram the triangle shown is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/8580226d740573679014c7ed39242f5a06b7305a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 40 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 55 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 35 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 50 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aea3184063ae2117b4d51d0f980204525ce6005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC = m\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"14\" />. We can then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the value of these two angles.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> is always the sum of the interior angles in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a>, we can set up an equation involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c124302a78af220ce6d9c2611ec5ac811ab50775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC + m\\angle ACB + m\\angle BAC = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"312\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652cbe9982d174734e1a6a6d2fb33488eeef6f04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + y + 40 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb795cef2bbbaa9bb305768115ddef8550a672c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y + 40 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d01af361725f624184f53ce0bd82e4571389e595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y = 140$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98eba305be182b9822cc0561e42b07644a3cd350.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 70^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr /> \n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> then form a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">straight angle</a>, allowing us to set up an equation involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8e76bf139e43fb87d76d0dbc9095737848a2f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + y = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181d55f2e17499b567f44079c02a21f7654fef19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 70 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/4150c3e8ebf2e0ae3a27c6ab8a33b3564fde242f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c4867e7c75789f00147be03b9c6dde82e2ba0cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 55}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca31e293b762acfa9b4ec1b10003041fbcc0bcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ACB = 180 - (m\\angle ABC + m\\angle BAC) = 180 - (y + 40)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"464\" height=\"20\" />, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a50f116e03e32035702fb7842b9cebdcee30c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 180 - (180 - (y + 40)) = y + 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We can use the same process as solution 1 to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98eba305be182b9822cc0561e42b07644a3cd350.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 70^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, so:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/335d5539938374c68f7e61388e8e0d0f5fb8333c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 70 + 40 = 110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c4867e7c75789f00147be03b9c6dde82e2ba0cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 55}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Test_Errors\">Test Errors</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Test Errors\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is listed twice in the answer choices.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal\">1997 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5